    {
      "@id": "urn:adk-prov:runs/data/0fe4a346411a42489132f575225b9abf",
      "@type": "lcont:LLMResponse",
      "dcterms:title": "response:InventoryDrafter_agent",
      "prov:value": "Excellent! I've loaded the complete 7-step synthesis route for Octocrylene. Now I'll build a comprehensive draft LCI with all intermediate nodes, proper stoichiometry, and mandatory biosphere exchanges.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"inventory\": {\n    \"name\": \"Octocrylene production, GLO\",\n    \"comment\": \"Complete 7-step synthesis route for Octocrylene (2-ethylhexyl 2-cyano-3,3-diphenylprop-2-enoate), a UV filter for cosmetics. Step 1: Knoevenagel condensation (ethyl cyanoacetate + benzophenone → Etocrylene). Step 2: Acetoacetic ester alkylation (ethyl acetoacetate + butyl bromide → ethyl 2-acetylhexanoate). Step 3: Selective ketone reduction (ethyl 2-acetylhexanoate + H2 → ethyl 2-(1-hydroxyethyl)hexanoate). Step 4: Ester hydrolysis (ethyl 2-(1-hydroxyethyl)hexanoate + H2O → 2-(1-hydroxyethyl)hexanoic acid). Step 5: Diol formation (2-(1-hydroxyethyl)hexanoic acid + CH4 → 2-butylbutane-1,3-diol). Step 6: Decarbonylation (2-butylbutane-1,3-diol + CO → 2-ethylhexanol + CO2). Step 7: Transesterification (Etocrylene + 2-ethylhexanol → Octocrylene + ethanol). Normalized to 1 kg Octocrylene reference product.\",\n    \"source\": \"InventoryDrafter_agent\",\n    \"nodes\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"octocrylene_production\",\n        \"name\": \"Octocrylene production\",\n        \"unit\": \"kg\",\n        \"type\": {\n          \"name\": \"process\"\n        },\n        \"location\": {\n          \"code\": \"GLO\"\n        },\n        \"code\": \"default_code\",\n        \"database\": \"default_database\",\n        \"source\": \"InventoryDrafter_agent\",\n        \"product_information\": \"2-Ethylhexyl 2-cyano-3,3-diphenylprop-2-enoate. UV filter for cosmetics and sunscreens.\",\n        \"comment\": \"Transesterification of Etocrylene with 2-ethylhexanol. Acid-catalyzed at 60-120°C under atmospheric to slightly elevated pressure. Catalyst: TiCl4, SnCl2, or p-toluenesulfonic acid (0.1-1 wt%). Solvent: Toluene/Xylene. Reaction time: 2-8 hours. Ethanol