    {
      "@id": "urn:adk-prov:runs/data/eceb74ceedeb4410be2eb312d66cb60a",
      "@type": "lcont:LLMResponse",
      "dcterms:title": "response:ProcessDescriptor_agent",
      "prov:value": "```json\n{\n  \"success\": \"This reaction represents a deoxidative decarbonylation process converting a diol to a primary alcohol using carbon monoxide as a reducing agent.\\n\\n**PROCESS OVERVIEW:**\\nThe reaction transforms 2-butylbutane-1,3-diol (a bifunctional diol) into 2-ethylhexan-1-ol by selective removal of one hydroxyl group via decarbonylation, with CO as the reducing agent and CO2 as a byproduct.\\n\\n**KEY PROCESS PARAMETERS:**\\n\\n**Catalytic System:**\\n- Transition metal catalysts required, likely rhodium (Rh) or other precious metal-based systems\\n- Typical catalyst loading: 0.5-5 mol% based on diol substrate\\n- Common catalyst precursors: HRh(CO)(PPh3)3 (Wilkinson's catalyst) or similar phosphine-stabilized systems\\n\\n**Reaction Conditions:**\\n- Temperature: 100-150°C (moderate heating to facilitate decarbonylation)\\n- Pressure: 1-5 atm CO atmosphere (carbon monoxide supply critical)\\n- Solvent: Aromatic hydrocarbons (toluene, xylene) or ethers (THF, dioxane) to solubilize both reactants and catalyst\\n- Reaction time: 2-12 hours depending on temperature and catalyst efficiency\\n\\n**Thermodynamic Profile:**\\n- Energy requirement: Endothermic process; external heat input necessary\\n- Driving force: Formation of CO2 (thermodynamically favorable)\\n- Equilibrium considerations: Continuous CO supply shifts equilibrium toward products\\n\\n**Industrial Considerations:**\\n- CO handling: Requires specialized equipment with inert atmosphere/positive pressure control\\n- Safety: CO is toxic and flammable; closed systems with proper ventilation essential\\n- Selectivity: Selective reduction of secondary hydroxyl group over primary (steric factors)\\n- Byproduct: CO2 removal via purge gas or vacuum\\n- Yield optimization: Controlled stoichiometric ratio of reactants and catalyst efficiency critical\\n- Scale-up: Requires stirred autoclave reactors with precise temperature/pressure control and gas flow regulation\\n\\n**INDUSTRIAL RELEVANCE:**\\nThis transformation is relevant to specialty alcohol production for plasticizers, detergents, and pharmaceutical intermediates where selective deoxygenation of polyols is needed while preserving terminal primary alcohols.\"\n}\n```",
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "urn:adk-prov:runs/prompt/ProcessDescriptor_agent_process_completion_d41d8cd98f00b204"
      },
      "prov:wasGeneratedBy": {
        "@id": "urn:adk-prov:runs/process/b01d06ca07bf46ec91dd3dee990871af"
      }
    },
