    {
      "@id": "urn:adk-prov:runs/data/a1c31d34150c4b5fb615f5cc64a4d685",
      "@type": "lcont:LLMResponse",
      "dcterms:title": "response:BW2LCIbuilder_agent",
      "prov:value": "Perfect! ✅\n\n## Summary\n\nI have successfully built a Brightway2 2.5 compliant Life Cycle Inventory for **Octocrylene** located in **EUR**. The inventory has been validated and is now ready for use.\n\n### Key Results:\n\n**Inventory Structure:**\n- **Main Product Node**: Octocrylene production (foreground_fallback, EUR location, 1 kg reference)\n- **Sub-system Node**: Etocrylene production (foreground_fallback, upstream intermediate)\n- **Ecoinvent-Matched Nodes** (6 total):\n  - 2-Ethylhexanol (RER, ecoinvent-3.12-cutoff)\n  - Ethanol (RER, from ethylene)\n  - Toluene (RER, liquid solvent)\n  - Piperidine (RER, catalyst)\n  - Dimethylformamide (RER, solvent)\n  - Electricity, medium voltage (RER utility)\n  - Heat, process (RER utility)\n\n**Production System:**\nThe inventory captures the key final synthesis step (Step 7 in the original draft):\n- **Transesterification reaction**: Etocrylene + 2-Ethylhexanol → Octocrylene + Ethanol (by-product credit)\n- **Catalyst**: TiCl4 (0.5 wt%)\n- **Solvent**: Toluene (30% recovered)\n- **Utilities**: Electricity (0.8 kWh/kg) and Heat (2.5 MJ/kg)\n- **Emissions**: CO₂ (0.15 kg/kg) and Waste water (0.1 kg/kg)\n\n**Validation Status**: ✅ VALID (9 nodes, all exchanges properly linked, all external codes verified)\n\nThe inventory is now saved to `/home/cogoni/Workspace/PINK/pink-chemlcibuilder/data/outputs/json/Octocrylene/74268b26/bw_inventory.json` and ready for LCIA calculations.",
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
