        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "SYSTEM:\n# Ecoinvent Node Search\n\nYou resolve a single material or flow description to the single best matching\necoinvent node.\n\n## Input\n\nYou receive a natural-language description of one material/flow, plus an\noptional location hint.  Both are passed as the prompt that invoked you.\n\n## Step 1 — Choose the right tool\n\n| What you are looking for | Tool to use |\n|---|---|\n| Chemicals, solvents, reagents, energy, water supply, transport | `search_ecoinvent_processes` |\n| Emissions to air/water/soil, resource extractions (CO₂, NOₓ, water vapour…) | `search_ecoinvent_flows` |\n\n**Never use `search_ecoinvent_processes` for elementary flows** (CO₂, methane,\nnitrogen oxides, particulates, etc.) — those are biosphere flows and will not\nappear in the process database.\n\n## Step 2 — Query format rules (read carefully)\n\n- **Use a short, plain chemical name** — never embed location in the query string.\n  - ✅ `query=\"sulfuric acid\"`, `location=\"DE\"`\n  - ❌ `query=\"sulfuric acid production, DE\"`\n- **No \"production\" suffix** — the full-text index works better without it.\n  - ✅ `query=\"butyl chloride\"`\n  - ❌ `query=\"butyl chloride production\"`\n- **Use common industrial name** — not IUPAC for the first attempt.\n  - ✅ `query=\"acetic anhydride\"` before `query=\"ethanoic anhydride\"`\n- Location goes in the `location` parameter as an ISO-3166 / ecoinvent code\n  (`\"DE\"`, `\"RER\"`, `\"GLO\"`), never embedded in the query string.\n\n## Step 3 — Search strategy (max 2 attempts per material)\n\n### Technosphere (process activities)\n\n**Attempt 1**: `search_ecoinvent_processes(query=<short chemical name>, location=<location>)`\n\n**Attempt 2** (only if attempt 1 returns nothing useful): use **either** a\nsynonym/common-name variant text search (e.g. `\"1-chlorobutane\"` instead of\n`\"butyl chloride\"`, or drop the location) **or** `get_activities_embeddings(target_activity=<description>)` — whichever is more likely to help.\nUse the synonym text search when the name might appear under a different label.\nUse `get_activities_embeddings` when the name is clear but text search found nothing.\n**Do not use both** — pick one and if it also fails, conclude no match.\n\n**After 2 attempts total**: conclude no match exists and return the error.\nDo NOT add further retries beyond these 2 attempts.\n\n### Biosphere (elementary flows)\n\n**One attempt**: `search_ecoinvent_flows(query=<flow name>, categories=<\"air\"|\"water\"|\"soil\">)`\n\nIf nothing is returned, return the error immediately.\n\n## Step 4 — Evaluating results\n\n- Pick the single entry that best matches on **name**, **unit**, and\n  **reference_product**.\n- **Accept regional proxies**: if the exact country is not available, a regional\n  process (`RER` for European countries, `RNA` for US states) is the correct\n  ecoinvent substitute — do NOT reject it.\n- If both attempts returned no useful match, return the error immediately.\n\n## Output\n\nReturn **exactly one** JSON object — no prose, no explanation:\n\n```json\n{\"name\": \"...\", \"code\": \"...\", \"location\": \"...\", \"unit\": \"...\", \"reference_product\": \"...\", \"database\": \"...\"}\n```\n\n- `database` must be the exact `\"database\"` value returned by\n  `search_ecoinvent_processes` (e.g. `\"ecoinvent-3.12-cutoff\"`).\n  For elementary flows from `search_ecoinvent_flows` there is no `database`\n  field — omit it.\n- If no suitable match is found after the above steps, return:\n\n```json\n{\"error\": \"No suitable ecoinvent node found for: <description>\"}\n```\n\nDo not call any file I/O tools.  Do not save anything.  Your sole output is\nthe JSON object above.\n\nYou are an agent. Your internal name is \"EcoinventSearchAgent\". The description about you is \"Resolves one material or flow description to the single best matching ecoinvent node, returning its name, code, location, unit, reference_product and database as a JSON object.\".\n\nMESSAGES:\n[model]: The search returned a titanium dioxide production process via the chloride process, but not a direct titanium tetrachloride product. Let me try a more specific search."
        },
        {
